            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "I've verified the Redfish URI structure and the EnvironmentMetrics implementation. The power limit properties are correctly exposed under the Processor resource as expected.\n\n# Verified Processor resource links to EnvironmentMetrics\n$ curl -k -u root:0penBmc -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -X GET https://\"${BMC}\"/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Processors/GPU_*_*\n{\n  \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Processors/GPU_*_*\",\n  \"@odata.type\": \"#Processor.v1_18_0.Processor\",\n  ...\n  \"EnvironmentMetrics\": {\n    \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Processors/GPU_*_*/EnvironmentMetrics\"\n  },\n  ...\n}\n\n# Verified EnvironmentMetrics content and PowerLimitWatts properties\n$ curl -k -u root:0penBmc -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -X GET https://\"${BMC}\"/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Processors/GPU_*_*/EnvironmentMetrics\n{\n  \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Processors/GPU_*_*/EnvironmentMetrics\",\n  \"@odata.type\": \"#EnvironmentMetrics.v1_3_0.EnvironmentMetrics\",\n  \"Id\": \"EnvironmentMetrics\",\n  \"Name\": \"Processor Environment Metrics\",\n  \"PowerLimitWatts\": {\n    \"AllowableMax\": {},\n    \"AllowableMin\": {},\n    \"ControlMode\": {},\n    \"DefaultSetPoint\": {},\n    \"SetPoint\": {}\n  }\n}\n\nThe results look good."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Could you rebase on the latest 87018? It removed afterGetProcessorForEnvMetrics.\nHappy to help if useful. Thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 345,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "please use the generated ControlMode enum here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 345,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "There is not an existing operator to compare a string to an enum. I did not find an example of elsewhere we use the generated enum for comparison. Do you know of an example. I could create a mapping function, but that seems like it just ends up obfuscating the comparison since it is not used elsewhere.\n\n../../../../../../workspace/sources/bmcweb/redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp:358:26: error: no match for 'operator==' (operand types are 'const std::string' {aka 'const std::__cxx11::basic_string<char>'} and 'control::ControlMode')\n  358 |     else if (controlMode == control::ControlMode::Automatic)\n      |              ~~~~~~~~~~~ ^~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n      |              |                                    |\n      |              |                                    control::ControlMode\n      |              const std::string {aka const std::__cxx11::basic_string<char>}"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 345,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for checking \u2014 no problem, this is fine as-is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 551,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we keep `messages::internalError(asyncResp->res);` here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 551,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "The intention here was for the callback() function to handle reporting an error back to the user if appropriate. For GET no error is reported if no single object is found. For PATCH an error would be reported.\n\nIt could be argued the ec should be set for the size > 1 case, is that what you are asking for? If so, what error do you suggest?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 551,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes \u2014 for the size > 1 case please set internalError (server-side misconfig: a single controlled_by shouldn't map to multiple Power.Cap objects). The empty-subtree case keeping the silent callback is fine; it's only size > 1 I'd surface as 500"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 551,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Added the internalError() here and changed the message back to ERROR.\n\nNote: This special-case will not call the callback to handle the error since it is being treated as an internal error here. I've updated the commit message to call out this special-case."
                }
            ],
