                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "When both setPoint and controlMode are set and the lookup failed (ec), both setters run their own ec check and each emit propertyUnknown, so the response carries it twice. \nConsider one ec/empty check here before dispatching."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/environment_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 370,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point. I'm moving the ec check into this function. The error message includes the property name so I'm changing it to \"PowerLimitWatts\" since if the object does not exist then none of these properties are modifiable. (Also necessary to handle the case that both properties are specified in the request.)\n\nIncorrect values for the different settings are still handled separately."
                }
            ],
